{"editorial_reason":"An indexed product topology begins with each topological factor (X_i,τ_i), so the independently screened topological-space definition supplies its coordinate open sets. The cylinder-preimage family is a SUBBASIS, not the topology itself.","from_formulation":"form.wave2.branch129.indexed-product-topology.1","human_verified":false,"id":"rel.wave2.branch130.01","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_product_eigen_graph_egf_direct_dependency_screen_2026_10_20","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AProduct_Topology","source_phrase":"topological spaces","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ATopological_Space","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.topological-space"}
{"editorial_reason":"Each product-coordinate projection π_i:X→X_i is a map taking a tuple to its ith entry. The source-specific mapping definition supplies its total single-valued behavior, used in the inverse-image cylinder subbasis.","from_formulation":"form.wave2.branch129.indexed-product-topology.1","human_verified":false,"id":"rel.wave2.branch130.02","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_product_eigen_graph_egf_direct_dependency_screen_2026_10_20","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AProduct_Topology","source_phrase":"projection","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AMapping","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.mapping-element-assignment"}
{"editorial_reason":"The finite-support open product basis uses open sets U_i of a topological space X_i in each coordinate, with all but finitely many unrestricted. The independently reviewed topology meaning supplies precisely those factor open subsets.","from_formulation":"form.wave2.branch129.indexed-product-topology.2","human_verified":false,"id":"rel.wave2.branch130.03","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_product_eigen_graph_egf_direct_dependency_screen_2026_10_20","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AProduct_Topology","source_phrase":"topological spaces","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ATopological_Space","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.topological-space"}
{"editorial_reason":"An eigenvalue of A requires a K-linear endomorphism A:V→V so the shifted map A−λI_V is linear and type-correct. The separately sourced field-linear transformation meaning supplies the K-linear structure, with equal domain and codomain specified.","from_formulation":"form.wave2.branch129.operator-eigenvalue.1","human_verified":false,"id":"rel.wave2.branch130.04","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_product_eigen_graph_egf_direct_dependency_screen_2026_10_20","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AEigenvalue","source_phrase":"K-linear operator","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ALinear_Transformation","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.cross110.field-vector-linear"}
{"editorial_reason":"The scalar λ is an eigenvalue exactly when the K-linear shifted operator A−λI_V has a kernel containing a NONZERO vector. The independently screened linear-map kernel definition supplies that preimage-of-zero construction.","from_formulation":"form.wave2.branch129.operator-eigenvalue.1","human_verified":false,"id":"rel.wave2.branch130.05","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_product_eigen_graph_egf_direct_dependency_screen_2026_10_20","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AEigenvalue","source_phrase":"ker(A−λI_V)","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AKernel_of_Linear_Transformation","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.cross107.field-vector-linear-kernel"}
{"editorial_reason":"The equivalent existence of v≠0 with A(v)=λv presupposes the same field-linear map from V to itself. This source-grounded target supplies the linear assignment; nonzero eigenvectors are witnesses, not the eigenvalue itself.","from_formulation":"form.wave2.branch129.operator-eigenvalue.2","human_verified":false,"id":"rel.wave2.branch130.06","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_product_eigen_graph_egf_direct_dependency_screen_2026_10_20","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AEigenvalue","source_phrase":"K-linear endomorphism","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ALinear_Transformation","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.cross110.field-vector-linear"}
{"editorial_reason":"The witness v lies in the K-vector space V and must be nonzero; λ acts by field scalar multiplication. The independently sourced vector-space target supplies addition, scalar multiplication and its zero element.","from_formulation":"form.wave2.branch129.operator-eigenvalue.2","human_verified":false,"id":"rel.wave2.branch130.07","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_product_eigen_graph_egf_direct_dependency_screen_2026_10_20","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AEigenvalue","source_phrase":"nonzero v","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09FM","target_meaning":"meaning.b64bc15f46fe0245.vector-space-over-field"}
{"editorial_reason":"The connectivity predicate quantifies over pairs of vertices in a simple undirected graph with two-element unordered edges. The independently screened graph target supplies vertices and edges, while this definition explicitly restricts V to nonempty.","from_formulation":"form.wave2.branch129.nonempty-connected-graph","human_verified":false,"id":"rel.wave2.branch130.08","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_product_eigen_graph_egf_direct_dependency_screen_2026_10_20","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AConnected_%28Graph_Theory%29/Graph","source_phrase":"simple undirected graph","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ASimple_Graph","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.graph42.simple-undirected"}
{"editorial_reason":"The analytic exponential generating function evaluates the power series with real coefficients b_n=a_n/n! and center zero. The independently screened centered real-power-series meaning supplies its unevaluated expression, but does not alone imply convergence.","from_formulation":"form.wave2.branch129.real-convergent-egf","human_verified":false,"id":"rel.wave2.branch130.09","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_product_eigen_graph_egf_direct_dependency_screen_2026_10_20","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AExponential_Generating_Function","source_phrase":"∑","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3APower_Series/Real_Domain","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.prereq122.real-centered-power-series"}
{"editorial_reason":"The domain of the exponential generating function comprises exactly real z for which the numeric series sum of b_n z^n has a finite real limit. The separately reviewed convergent-series meaning supplies convergence of partial sums.","from_formulation":"form.wave2.branch129.real-convergent-egf","human_verified":false,"id":"rel.wave2.branch130.10","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_product_eigen_graph_egf_direct_dependency_screen_2026_10_20","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AExponential_Generating_Function","source_phrase":"converges","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AConvergent_Series","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.prereq122.real-series-convergent"}
{"editorial_reason":"Unlike a purely formal EGF, the definition here is an actual typed real-valued map E_A:D→R on the convergent locus D. The independently sourced mapping meaning supplies that input-to-unique-output assignment.","from_formulation":"form.wave2.branch129.real-convergent-egf","human_verified":false,"id":"rel.wave2.branch130.11","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_product_eigen_graph_egf_direct_dependency_screen_2026_10_20","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AExponential_Generating_Function","source_phrase":"E_A:D→ℝ","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AMapping","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.mapping-element-assignment"}
{"editorial_reason":"The real sequence coefficients, real argument z and finite real-valued power series sum require the real field, not merely a generic coefficient ring. The independently screened real-number meaning supplies the required scalar setting.","from_formulation":"form.wave2.branch129.real-convergent-egf","human_verified":false,"id":"rel.wave2.branch130.12","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_product_eigen_graph_egf_direct_dependency_screen_2026_10_20","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AExponential_Generating_Function","source_phrase":"ℝ","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AReal_Number","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.real45.complete-ordered-real-field"}
